    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15213#issuecomment-6772796024\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15213\">PR #15213</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The limitation of <code>max_io_size</code> is pretty broadly placing a limit on the size of the allocation made when copying between the guest and the host. Here, though, this is already host-allocated bytes so there's no real purpose in limiting it. Is there a missing clamp before this method is called though?</p>\n</blockquote>",
